From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 23:16:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 15/78] Do not enable excess precision by default in Delphi
 mode

Delphi mode turned on cs_excessprecision, which evaluates every float
expression in pbestrealtype: the x87 Extended type on x86_64-linux. All
Delphi-mode Single and Double arithmetic then compiled to x87 code: values
are double rounded, intermediates get the Extended exponent range
(1e308*10/10 gives 1e308 instead of overflowing), and code that masks
float exceptions through MXCSR (SetSSECSR) traps on x87 exceptions. 3.2
leaves excess precision off; {$EXCESSPRECISION ON} still enables it.
---
 compiler/scanner.pas | 12 ++++++------
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/compiler/scanner.pas b/compiler/scanner.pas
index 34c4cf09..871565fb 100644
--- a/compiler/scanner.pas
+++ b/compiler/scanner.pas
@@ -696,16 +696,16 @@ implementation
                  include(init_settings.localswitches,cs_strict_var_strings);
              end;
 
-           { in delphi mode, excess precision and open strings are by default on }
+           { in delphi mode, open strings are by default on. Excess precision
+             stays off as in 3.2: it evaluates every float expression in
+             pbestrealtype, which is the x87 Extended type on x86_64-linux,
+             so Delphi-mode code would leave SSE for x87 code with its own
+             exception mask and double rounding; use $EXCESSPRECISION ON }
            if ([m_delphi] * current_settings.modeswitches <> []) then
              begin
-               include(current_settings.localswitches,cs_excessprecision);
                include(current_settings.localswitches,cs_openstring);
                if changeinit then
-                 begin
-                   include(init_settings.localswitches,cs_excessprecision);
-                   include(init_settings.localswitches,cs_openstring);
-                 end;
+                 include(init_settings.localswitches,cs_openstring);
              end;
 
 {$ifdef i8086}
